    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0263" n="151" xml:id="pg151"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/1963</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-21T15:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 21, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your August 17, 5 p.m. Should attempt be made to put the proposed regulations
                    into force you will make protest as suggested upon the basis of the Department’s
                    telegraphic instruction of October 13, 2 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d136-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
